build/
*.fjm
!versions/*.fjm
assets/doom1.wad
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
assets/freedoom1.wad
assets/freedoom2.wad
assets/freedoom-*.zip
assets/freedoom-*/

# the 12M campaign's build artifacts: one 25 MB label table and an 11 MB image PER IDEA.
# The numbers that matter live in scratchpad/12m/{LEDGER,FINDINGS,ATLAS}.md, which ARE tracked.
scratchpad/12m/atlas/
scratchpad/12m/bak/

# ── scratchpad byproducts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MEASURED 2026-09-11: 1,107 untracked files and 3,509 MB of them, against 0.7 MB of .py. Two
# label dumps were 683 MB EACH. Every one is something a tool in scratchpad/ produced and can
# produce again; what was learned from them lives in scratchpad/12m/FINDINGS.md, which is tracked.
# A `git status` that lists 1,472 files is a `git status` nobody reads, and that is how a real
# change hides.
#
# ⚠ THESE RULES ONLY GOVERN NEW FILES. 134 .log and 3 .png under scratchpad/ are ALREADY TRACKED
# and stay tracked -- gitignore does not untrack anything. Removing them is a separate decision.
# ⚠ .py IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED. Probes get cannibalised into real tools, and a tool whose
# output is quoted as proof must be committed (docs/cr-rules.md R9).
scratchpad/**/*.json
scratchpad/**/*.gz
scratchpad/**/*.fj
scratchpad/**/*.fjm
scratchpad/**/*.bin
scratchpad/**/*.jsonl
scratchpad/**/*.csv
scratchpad/**/*.tsv
scratchpad/**/*.diff
scratchpad/**/*.bak
scratchpad/**/*.png
scratchpad/**/*.gif
scratchpad/**/*.err
scratchpad/**/*.log
# ...except the counts cache, which is 0.4 MB and saves ~13 minutes and a whole assembly on the
# next blocked build (build_blocked.py --counts-cache; it self-invalidates when the emitter moves).
!scratchpad/12m/_counts_game.json.gz
